        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Iqbal F. Qadir\n- Events: Second war with India, attack on the Dwarka radar station\n- Places: Dwarka, India, Okhamandal Peninsula, Gomti River\n\nFacts:\n- Iqbal F. Qadir is renowned for participating in the second war with India.\n- Iqbal F. Qadir was part of the flotilla that attacked the radar station in Dwarka, India.\n- Dwarka is located on the western shore of the Okhamandal Peninsula.\n- Dwarka is located on the right bank of the Gomti River.",
